  "slug": "hall-quantum-4ded",
  "summary": "Five preprints trace Hall responses to orbital exchange, disorder, 3D Chern-number limits and pseudospin order in Bernal graphene, including hysteretic transitions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that Hall-type responses are attributed to orbital degrees of freedom, disorder and interactions rather than to spin magnetism or pristine band topology alone. Reported results include orbital Hall currents generated by structural and electrostatic disorder, including in amorphous graphene, and intrinsic anomalous Hall conductivity from an orbital exchange field in spinless monolayer H-phase MoS2 without spin-orbit coupling. In 3D quantum anomalous Hall systems built from coupled Weyl semimetals, Chern numbers alone fail to characterize chiral behavior. In Bernal multilayer graphene, Hartree-Fock work predicts anomalous Hall metals from pseudospin ordering in the tetralayer, while experiments on the pentalayer show displacement-field-tunable first-order transitions with hysteretic Hall responses. What is new is treating disorder and orbital or pseudospin order as sources of Hall responses.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
